# L §4.2, E §3.1 (tally 2.1.6, issue #72): a schedule load sees that gives no date in the run (day 0 of every month)
# is refused at load whatever the asks: asking only an ask the base lacks prints LOAD-SCHEDULE, which outranks REQ-ASK
# (E §11). M0's fixture basic/schedule. tally 2.1.5's refcore refused it only where an ask reached the move, so it
# printed REQ-ASK here.
=== m.tally
model basic
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T's base for M0's load-code fixtures (invented): it loads clean; each fixture of codes/m0/edits.tsv changes one line"

source card "T's fixture card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index qs = [q1, q2]

index qm = month 2026-02..2026-02

input cal: calendar

move rent[m in qm]: transfers
  on schedule(m, 0, unadjusted, cal)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

input amt: money PLN

input day: date

input rate[k in qs]: num

def fee[k in qs]: money PLN
  rule base v card_2026 = round(amt * rate[k], minor(PLN), half-up)
  rule waived beats base v card_2026 = 0 PLN when rate[k] == 0

def total: money PLN = sum(fee[k] for k in qs)

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay: transfers
  on day
  leg cash from konto to world amount fee[q1]

ask q: total, bal(konto, 2026-12-31), flows(rent, 2026)

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "the card"
  day = 2026-02-10 "the card"
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun]) "the card"
  rate[q1] = 0.1 "the card"
  rate[q2] = 0 "the card"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "the card"
=== expect zz_m0_probe
refused: LOAD-SCHEDULE schedule schedule(m, 0, unadjusted, cal) (the day of rent) gives no date in the run (m.tally:18)
